// src/v4/extdeps/languages/typescript.dag
//
// Scope: TypeScript language model — direction-agnostic. Includes ES (ECMAScript) base.
// Anchor: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html (TypeScript Handbook) + https://tc39.es/ecma262/ (ECMAScript spec)
// Unifies: (per THESIS:188) language spec = transport spec = interpreter runtime. ONE substrate carrier for all three roles. Different lenses read different facts from the same data (emission reads syntax; transport reads serialization; interpreter reads execution semantics). A worker needing transport or runtime extends this file, not a new "transport spec" file.
//
// Owns:
//   - TypeScript grammar (declarations, expressions, types, generics, interfaces, classes)
//   - Structural type system (TS uses structural typing, not nominal)
//   - Inhabitance: number -> ApproximateField (TS `number` IS an IEEE-754
//     double — NOT an exact Field: rounding breaks associativity and
//     distributivity. Same grounding as std/algebra.dag `Float ->
//     ApproximateField`; per MODELING.md M9, `number` IS the Float
//     concept and must attach to that existing algebra, not a fresh
//     exact-Field claim), string -> FreeMonoid<char>, Array<T> -> List<T>
//   - Cost realization: per-operation cost on TypeScript / JavaScript targets
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/algebra.dag, std/primitive.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-4
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.extdeps.languages.typescript

